{# TEAM › PERMISSIONS — the frame every Permissions page wears.

   THE HEAD IS THE PAGE'S OWN: the title, the one sentence under it, the
   "Super Admin only" chip and what the page says about the run (Recompute
   now on the hub). The section's Configure is not in it: the design's head
   carries none, so this frame writes the head rather than the shell's
   default, which appends it.

   THE STRIP IS THE SHELL'S, from TeamSectionTabs, which answers the hub's
   two tabs on the hub and the lookups' three on a lookup. #}
{% extends '@Shell/page.html.twig' %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {{ include('@Team/_stylesheets.html.twig') }}
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_subtitle %}What every kind of person may do to every other, asked of the rules the app enforces &mdash; for real accounts, changing nothing.{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_head %}
    <div>
        <h1 class="pg">{{ _title }}</h1>
        <p class="pgsub">{{ _subtitle }}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pgact w-pgact"><span class="chip acc">Super Admin only</span>{% block permissions_run %}{% endblock %}</div>
{% endblock %}
